    <h2 class="hs">Communication practice</h2>
    <p>Sharpening the stakeholder half of the job. I work through <a href="https://www.fastersmarter.io/">Think Fast Talk Smart</a> — a long-form podcast hosted by Matt Abrahams, a lecturer of Strategic Communication at Stanford Graduate School of Business. 300+ episodes on structured communication: answering questions on the spot, speaking under pressure, and explaining complicated things to people who don’t share your context.</p>
    <p>Most of what I write as requirements has to survive being said out loud first — in workshops, in UAT, in a client call. This is the closest thing I have to reps for that part of the role, and it feeds straight into how I scope things, write acceptance criteria, and run refinement.</p>
    <div class="chips"><span>Structured communication</span><span>Handling questions</span><span>Speaking under pressure</span><span>Clear writing</span><span>Presenting to stakeholders</span></div>
